= District Development Council elections announced

Nominations have been called for the upcoming District Development Council elections by the government. 

Resulting from the 1979 Tennakoon Commission and demands from the TULF to address Tamil concerns, the UNP proposed the DDC's as their solution.

24 of these councils are to be formed for each district, made up of elected members and local members of parliament overseen by a District Minister appointed by the central government and an elected chairman of the council.

The TULF has actively been working with the UNP to see through the necessary legislation. The TULF's participation in the elections has drawn criticism from the militants with the LTTE and EPRLF calling for a boycott from Tamils. 

The CPSL, LSSP and NSSP have all decided to boycott the elections citing the UNP's "authoritarian" methods and critised the DDC's as a hollow attempt at addressing local concerns. They also note the actions taken last year against Mrs Sirimavo as proof of the UNP reppression of dissent and opposition.

The JVP has taken the opposite stance deciding to fully participate in the elections. This can be seen as apart of the JVP's opening to parliamentary democracy? or is this pragmatic in nature?

Our party is still in chaos with Sirimavo's position as leader in dispute and the internal factions bikkering, if we did participate we will be incredibly ineffective, but even to take part may be worth it, to at least show to the people that the SLFP can put a fight.

- @yes: The SLFP will participate in the DDC elections, our nominations will be handed over soon.
- @no: The SLFP calls for a boycott of the sham elections.

@no
on-arrival: ddc_elections_boycott = 1; in_election = 1;

Our decsion has brought further internal feuding. The Nationalists argued in favour of taking part. Nevertheless we are making a stand against these "elections".
  
@yes
on-arrival: ddc_elections_boycott = 0; left_dissent += 14; nationalist_dissent += 10; in_election = 1;

With our announcment we need to make our nominations for the councils. Already internal fueding is making this a difficult proccess, not to mention several members who want us to boycott the election, thess calls are particularily from the Left who want to stand in solidarity with Mrs Bandaranaike and the other left parties.

- @supportlssp: Should we get the support of the LSSP?
- @supportcpsl: Should we get the support of the CPSL?
- @supportnssp: Should we get the support of the NSSP?
- @end: Thats all the support we need.

@supportlssp
choose-if: lssp_relation >=54.9
unavailable-subtitle: The LSSP does not trust us enough
on-arrival: lsspbacking = 1; left_strenght +=3;
go-to: end

While the LSSP will not participate in the elections, they have agreed to endorse our nominations. 

@supportcpsl
choose-if: cpsl_relation >=54.9
unavailable-subtitle: The CPSL does not trust us enough
on-arrival: cpslbacking = 1; left_strenght +=3;
go-to: end

While the CPSL will not participate in the elections, they have agreed to endorse our nominations. 

@supportnssp
choose-if: nssp_relation >=54.9
unavailable-subtitle: The NSSP does not trust us enough
on-arrival: nsspbacking = 1; left_strenght +=3;
go-to: end

While the NSSP will not participate in the elections, they have agreed to endorse our nominations. 

@end

Its time to campaign then